+    <h2>Reading lists and cookies</h2>
+    <p>When you change your reading list, the site saves article identifiers in a server-side session. A session cookie associates your browser with that list. We do not initialize an empty reading list merely because you visit a page. You can remove saved articles in the reading-list menu. Clearing site cookies disconnects this browser from the list; it does not itself delete server-side data.</p>
+
+    <h2>Other network requests</h2>
+    <p>Some articles and featured stories load images from external hosts, including Imgur and our featured-story service. These hosts receive the connection information needed to deliver those images. The site uses a no-referrer policy to avoid sending the referring page URL. Hosting providers may also keep operational request logs; this application does not configure their retention.</p>
+
+    <h2>Browser privacy boundaries</h2>
+    <p>We send headers that prevent document caching and ask supporting browsers to disable camera, microphone, location, motion sensors, and browsing-topics access. The application does not request those permissions.</p>
